{%- comment -%}
<page>.md, alongside the <page>/index.md that md-mirror.liquid emits.

The ecosystem is split on which shape a markdown mirror lives at: Stripe and
Anthropic docs serve <page>.md, Cloudflare Docs serves <page>/index.md and 404s the
other. This site served only the second, so /intro.md returned a 404 with a
16,509-byte HTML body while /intro/index.md returned 3,172 bytes of markdown — and
`Accept: text/markdown` on the HTML URL returns text/html, so there was no
negotiation fallback either. Belt and braces, not a lost majority.

`remove_last: '/'` rather than a slice: `{{ doc.url }}` always ends in a slash, and
this is the only Liquid filter that trims exactly one trailing one. The root page is
not in `collections.contentMd` (it is an HTML template, mirrored by hand from
src/org/mirrors/home.liquid), so this never has to produce ".md" from "/".

NOT _redirects — src/org/_redirects documents Cloudflare Pages' 100-rule ceiling,
and in a static build a second copy of a file is free. 1,234 extra files, ~2 MB.
{%- endcomment -%}
